Games\" and \"Apps\" as top-level categories, with subcategories like \"Action,\" \"Strategy,\" \"Tools,\" \"Social,\" and \"Productivity\". I\'ll prepare the seeded games, keeping these categories in mind. Then, I plan to develop `server.ts` alongside these considerations. I\'m focusing on Multer to handle file uploads.\n\n\n**Refining Admin Authentication**\n\nI\'m now refining the admin authentication logic. I\'ve realized we need a robust, two-pronged approach. I will utilize Supabase Auth `signUp` or `signInWithPassword` if the admin user exists in their Supabase configuration, with a fallback to .env configuration if their Supabase instance hasn\'t been configured or the admin hasn\'t created a user!\n\n\n**Securing Local Admin Access**\n\nI\'ve implemented a fallback mechanism for admin authentication, allowing immediate login with environment credentials when Supabase is unavailable. I\'ll issue a signed session token to keep the login session active. Also, I\'ve confirmed that `/data/games.json` is the directory and file for local game data storage, and I\'ll include eight pre-defined games with Unsplash images. I am now working on seeding game image URLs.\n\n\n**Coding Server Functionality**\n\nI\'m now writing the complete `server.ts` file, and making sure it binds to port `3000` and host `0.0.0.0`. I\'m starting with Express setup, incorporating the JSON parser, and then configuring the static folder serving. I\'m setting `./dist` for production and `./public` and `./uploads` as static paths so that uploaded images in local mode are served correctly.\n\n\n"
