  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font and Theme**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the Tajawal font is correctly implemented, which gives us a strong base for modern Arabic text. Now I am dissecting the \"Professional Polish\" theme request, specifically isolating the design elements: colors, fonts, spacing, and borders.\n\n\n**Dissecting Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the Design HTML to extract the aesthetic core. I\'ve pinpointed the outer wrapper\'s background colors for both light and dark modes, along with text colors. Next, I\'m analyzing the header\'s specifications\342\200\224its height, background, and border\342\200\224to ensure a clean and professional appearance. The logo design is especially interesting, and I intend to work on implementing the visual elements as part of the theme, matching the user\'s branding.\n\n\n**Integrating Visual Elements**\n\nI\'ve examined the design, and identified a clean logo with a blue square and white rotated square that I\'ll integrate. Navigation text similar to Google Play is also important. More recently, I\'m focusing on the sidebar. The Design HTML features `dir=\"rtl\"` and an `<aside>` element. I\'m considering options: a sidebar layout, which is gorgeous, or a flexible design with a sidebar on desktops and horizontal scrolling on mobile.\n\n\n**Implementing Right Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the sidebar\'s implementation, and how the user\'s information should appear within it. I plan to construct a clean desktop sidebar on the right side with a border. It\'ll feature \"Store Category\" selection (All, Games, Apps) and dynamic sub-categories from the database, such as \"\330\243\331\204\330\271\330\247\330\250 \330\247\331\204\330\243\331\203\330\264\331\206\". There\'s also a button for \"\331\204\331\210\330\255\330\251 \330\247\331\204\330\245\330\257\330\247\330\261\330\251\" at the bottom. On desktops, the sidebar will be beautiful.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m making sure that the existing horizontal mobile layout remains comfortable, fully responsive, and works well on all devices, which is critical. I\'m focusing on the featured hero section, which is a great design element at the top of the store page, and it will be implemented in a dynamic way by pulling the first or highly rated game from the `games` list. I\'ll need to figure out how to incorporate the background gradient and image.\n\n\n**Defining Hero Section Logic**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the logic for the hero section\'s content. The aim is to showcase a \"\331\204\330\271\330\250\330\251 \330\247\331\204\330\243\330\263\330\250\331\210\330\271\" or \"\330\252\330\267\330\250\331\212\331\202 \330\247\331\204\330\243\330\263\330\250\331\210\330\271\" in a professional way. I\'m focusing on ensuring graceful handling of scenarios where no games meet the rating criteria by falling back to the first game in the list. I\'m excited about the approach I\'m taking to dynamically pull the featured game\'s title, description, and image and link everything. I will now integrate this using the featuredGame variable.\n\n\n"
