  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Build Success**\n\nThe build completed successfully, which is a significant relief! Now, my focus shifts to meticulously aligning the app\'s visual theme with the \"Professional Polish\" design specifications. My next steps involve extracting the styling elements\342\200\224colors, fonts, spacing, and borders\342\200\224to ensure a perfect match.\n\n\n**Analyzing Design Specifications**\n\nI am now thoroughly examining the Design HTML. My focus is on extracting key visual elements. I\'m noting the wrapper background colors and text colors, and the header\'s styles, including background, border, flexbox attributes, and padding. Currently I am updating the `src/App.tsx`\'s header to match. I\'m focusing on the logo and adjusting font sizes and alignments for active links, and I\'m ready to apply styling using the provided classes to the custom icon box.\n\n\n**Implementing Category Sync**\n\nI\'ve successfully mapped header link clicks to dynamically update the app state. Specifically, selecting \"\330\247\331\204\330\243\331\204\330\271\330\247\330\250\" now sets the store category to \"games\" and activates the \"store\" tab, the same for \"\330\247\331\204\330\252\330\267\330\250\331\212\331\202\330\247\330\252\". This ensures functional consistency. Next, I am working on the central input bar style with RTL and absolute icon. I\'m focusing on the user profile avatar style in the right container.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Strategy**\n\nI\'m now diving into the structural changes needed for the main app layout. I think I\'ll use `md:flex md:flex-row` for the store view on larger screens, to replicate the design with the sidebar. I am focusing on the discovery and categories section in the sidebar. I am thinking of adding \"\330\247\331\204\330\247\331\203\330\252\330\264\330\247\331\201\" as a header for discovery and \"\330\247\331\204\331\201\330\246\330\247\330\252\" for categories. I\'m focusing on \"\330\247\331\204\330\243\331\204\330