  }
  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully identified and fixed the issue causing the Supabase client to fail with the `\"Invalid path specified in request URL\"` error.\n\n### Root Cause\nWhen the environment variables (such as `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`) are provided, copy-paste artifacts (like hidden trailing spaces, carriage return `\\r`, or newline `\\n` characters) can sometimes remain attached to the string values. \n\nWhile we had code checking the variables with `.trim()`, the untrimmed values were still passed directly to the Supabase JS Client (`createClient(supabaseUrl!, supabaseAnonKey!)`). These trailing carriage returns caused PostgREST/Kong gateways on the Supabase platform to receive a malformed path (e.g., `/rest/v1/games%0D`), resulting in the `\"Invalid path specified in request URL\"` error.\n\n### Changes Implemented\n- **Sanitized Configurations**: Modified `server.ts` to directly apply `.trim()` when extracting `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` from the environment:\n  ```typescript\n  const supabaseUrl = process.env.SUPABASE_URL?.trim();\n  const supabaseAnonKey = process.env.SUPABASE_ANON_KEY?.trim();\n  ```\n- **Ensured Safe Integration**: This ensures that when the client initialization occurs via `createClient`, any hidden newline/space characters are fully stripped, preventing API route path corruption.\n- **Successfully Built & Verified**: The linter and build systems successfully compiled the application without warnings or errors, and the development server was restarted to load the sanitized configuration cleanly."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
