    summary: "The \"Invalid path specified in request URL\" error in Supabase typically indicates an issue with the URL being used in an API request, meaning the path does not match an expected format or resource. This error can manifest in various Supabase services, including Storage and Auth[1][2].\n\nCommon causes and solutions for this error include:\n\n*   **Incorrectly Formatted File Paths (Supabase Storage)**: When working with Supabase Storage, this error (sometimes appearing as `InvalidFilePath`) often means the file path provided is not correctly structured or contains unsupported characters.\n    *   **Solution**:\n        *   Verify the file path format: It should typically follow `bucket_name/folder_name/file_name.extension`. Ensure correct bucket, folder, and file names are used.[1]\n        *   Check for unsupported characters: Avoid special characters like `\\`, `:`, `*`, `?`, `\"`, `<`, `>`, and `|`.[1]\n        *   Validate path length: Ensure the path does not exceed the maximum allowed length.[1]\n\n*   **Misconfigured API Endpoint URL (Supabase Auth)**: For Supabase Auth, an \"Invalid API Endpoint\" error suggests a problem with the API endpoint URL itself.\n    *   **Solution**:\n        *   Verify the endpoint URL: Double-check for typographical errors, missing segments, or outdated URLs. The URL should match the format provided by Supabase (e.g., `https://your-project.supabase.co/auth/v1`).[2]\n        *   Check for API changes: If the endpoint previously worked, review Supabase documentation for any recent changes to the API structure or versioning.[2]\n        *   Ensure correct redirect URLs for OAuth: When using OAuth providers like Google, an \"Invalid path\" or `redirect_uri_mismatch` can occur if the redirect URLs configured in your Supabase project and the OAuth provider (e.g., Google Cloud Console) do not exactly match. This includes ensuring trailing slashes are consistent.[3][4]\n\n*   **General API Request Issues**: The error code `PGRST125` specifically denotes \"Invalid path is specified in request URL\" for general Supabase API requests.[5]\n    *   **Solution**:\n        *   Review your API request URL to ensure it corresponds to an existing table, view, or function in your Supabase project and follows the PostgREST conventions that Supabase uses.\n        *   If you are dealing with a local Supabase instance, ensure your application\'s URL configuration correctly points to it.[6]\n\n*   **Missing Trailing Slashes**: In some cases, a missing trailing slash in redirect URLs, particularly in authentication configurations, can lead to the \"Invalid path\" error.[4]\n    *   **Solution**: Add a trailing slash to the URL in your Supabase redirect URLs configuration.[4]\n\nIf you encounter this error, it\'s recommended to carefully review the exact URL being sent in your request, comparing it against the expected format for the specific Supabase service you are trying to access. Checking Supabase\'s official documentation and any related forum discussions or GitHub issues can also provide specific context and solutions.\n\nSources:\n[1] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQElF4DlHTqLBvthtt7ObHat0YZwmyc2hdWyIbIp6_NH_oVqt92wJPuP4E5wNlen2gEv05wcLWrv_KOtTxfvBNIDf_wvla5CmDVH8kX5a4A30t8J_kLCBbim58iLP_cBBYOlNYIlybEJJQ9gdzvEHpz5ixwVZhH0K3WXEo6UCK0ojf2MNiM8oWumO9_A1eL6c_Q_X0-XoWEBzCFPyNVktgfX6winvLLyMNt0bE-i6HAXoYhylh6RsPxP9XgW8jFg98u_bJPZ3D8cDaB1rL2_OA==)\n[2] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGP2elDC6FBkDcxq7XpDta4jhQpYqzZST6Obq2iRz--i0PDQ6RKvQPwthixivxacOxPIlS-OqqqWKPY2ezlYCkZV8UmJzMMCU4VSBOh4id5uLOBglQQjj03CGssZPnJGgwn5Nx86-6EHhFXbmWPyGQ_qyjo9QH9JxNj0pWLD4KvgQ==)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHTePgZfFxvWYIfG4yLYZFVuLwXoE1RKNrbsfIvKjn1viqX7frOomQB6N7QKcGYyGtZZ2BUjOeaoxDdZylWc8CxRexjyv5ToP5iDZh8iw2adBhk32ZKiPm0k2no6TzCJLP7M4D08ggATNP9pGVfvUy1D0rVJdAh1vuFVctk94MgobSXBiMnuLhySRnUTfIPj_TV8CgK4HoElOd-sq8ncLWpkWkYuzmiX5DalPHB8RcnjMixgl9OT4WO)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGcTtNMRO9mgE_sr80jSWKIxYKjFYQoNwALPXJXzVm4yYQujPfbWndBTyAn8Xo52PhgGiMi6IfUgrv6hUYPkqx18evbx8MJ_OXtyL9QD5AtNXCmOFzHJiJsN9iw7be_BOnIYw-oLJBIIbQDtrEWcW_GLBOewUn3Alc1BUX-Q9oiszigEeoQAxgp-6CS94a9AWmIx_-PCXmvFg==)\n[5] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGJWlvFk_3VF8QgLTs0N9E88bSFDbT0ODwJcBai3FcSd65D5uAHjJPNLMpnRdqOP47aAYFzjXDzyz8DrWytti3Zty8zvZig_hgekaVBSuJsr9jjurYI3VuXJunsz-Ly6JOYOyrhjA1MCqGin_tYoVM8_GI6zYcy2XnxCg==)\n[6] [nordcraft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHHt6W8B2eeTh-4NfxhCc_5P1Lp0D3PcOfzlRie1RcxzKUsfc_HP5OOPm7U_RC86BpyQtTlJas5zRgTpjhcAWn6f8B75_C3Y3VxuV-qUW09PRQsHYng-TM=)"
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
  }
