      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "The \"invalid path specified in request URL\" error in Supabase typically indicates a problem with how the Supabase client is configured or how API requests are structured. This error can manifest in various scenarios, including issues with authentication redirects, incorrect API endpoint usage, or malformed URLs in client-side code.\n\nHere are the common causes and solutions:\n\n*   **Incorrect Supabase URL or API Key**\n    *   **Using the PostgreSQL connection string**: A frequent mistake is using the direct PostgreSQL database connection string (which often starts with `postgresql://`) when initializing the Supabase client, instead of the project\'s HTTP Supabase URL. The `createClient` function requires the HTTP endpoint for API interactions.[1]\n    *   **Typographical errors**: Even minor typos in the `SUPABASE_URL` or `SUPABASE_KEY` environment variables can lead to this error.[2][3][4]\n    *   **Stale or incorrect keys**: Ensure that the API keys used in your application match the latest ones provided in your Supabase dashboard.[4][5]\n    *   **Missing environment variables**: Verify that `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_KEY` are correctly loaded and accessible in your application\'s environment.[6]\n\n*   **Authentication Redirect URL Misconfiguration**\n    *   **Unregistered redirect URLs**: For Supabase Auth, any redirect URLs used after a successful login or signup must be explicitly whitelisted in your Supabase project\'s authentication settings. If the URL is not in the allowed list, Supabase will block the redirection for security reasons.[7][3][5]\n    *   **Missing trailing slashes or incorrect wildcards**: In some cases, a missing trailing slash (e.g., `http://localhost:3000` instead of `http://localhost:3000/`) or an incorrect wildcard pattern in the redirect URL configuration can cause issues.[8]\n    *   **Platform-specific redirect issues**: When working with platforms like Expo Go, issues can arise if Supabase\'s redirect logic doesn\'t correctly handle the proxy URLs.[9]\n\n*   **API Endpoint Specific Problems**\n    *   **Invalid path (PGRST126 error)**: Supabase\'s PostgREST API can return a `PGRST126` error with a 404 HTTP status if an invalid path is specified in the request URL.[10]\n    *   **Missing or deprecated path segments**: The API endpoint URL might be incorrect due to missing segments, changes in the API structure, or the use of deprecated endpoints.[2]\n    *   **Incorrect HTTP verb for database functions**: For database functions, only `GET` and `POST` HTTP verbs are allowed. Using other verbs will result in an error.[10]\n    *   **Table not found**: If the table specified in the URI of a database query does not exist, it will lead to an error.[10]\n\n*   **Realtime Specific Errors**\n    *   **`TypeError: Invalid URL: undefined`**: This can occur when establishing a Realtime subscription if the base URL for the Supabase client contains extra characters (like a newline character) or if the client is not fully initialized before the Realtime call.[11]\n\n*   **General Troubleshooting Steps**\n    *   **Check project status**: Ensure your Supabase project is active and not paused, especially if you are on a free tier, as projects can automatically pause after inactivity.[4]\n    *   **Review dashboard logs**: The Supabase dashboard provides API call statistics and logs that can help pinpoint the exact nature of the error.[11]\n    *   **Network or IP bans**: A burst of failed connection attempts can temporarily block your client\'s IP address to protect the database from brute-force attacks.[4]\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-bOrZlV8Ez7l78gwlQXJ6W2xhT_8UAGwmuaiu0XpOv-Y_YgV1LludXb-hG0hSrXCojyYEQpsCTls1MTBokPksX_dGfxEyLaFvkENvQO9xXYkkn3sZC4-OAZcm106Pvo6uEnxl4a060bEohgkEiVF7ZT9ja9AHpcKGeXaHv8HbNFZUnl2USYHUD3TFQa12nCnOU52ejlfT2kfyI08o)\n[2] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFWe6rXky1RMY4kcV5EUvIGXyovtYOYzxVn_byv37wu2IGP2cODKBZAk5sVxUzSEM0CWj1JqSHeF64QyuYqK_cfnAa20eVv3KRpVv0K80qZBFjtIooBDHmZZ5uMRb0Mtfdo5AqMn94JUL_Ccz2XCoZfpqHrX-zPRcc0Y9EIHxoQcA==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHgguHAK48xKCh_u40zFLbIHEHmrFvKIDjPIYUqG901Ojn1oDCpLoXRlU1Y7o9wXBBgVUdl5t2VEc4YAWVndE1TO6BmxLagovtPiFNkGjuxV03NW1kKhGzK_z5lNqPPB0XLrwug152_mkeYv_R0)\n[4] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFfOMpVUWfuHC67V3svF1rDCS0ycOrRWoCBU1ZiAyjLcfcoWJVoNnUy34M7fRX-j2yBscvAXyzfXgEhm3_I_VpkAW1XLI8JK-bVVKkPSAU-gquFy_7moc6d3sf3HTC210xSYl18W9A=)\n[5] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGkmcODSpQyXz_EIheg97p_Z1pEs1N1fXb8QjtTFWT5Mn1Oh-W_uqkoxay1mKz5EhVHJPbhaI8WE5W1bKz8xG9glfOPUbvvnQp4BHED_RQJZDTd2YBawqDdurS-UkeKUdTy-_zGJyMHLULjYwXGq9MXfKEBDeXC9UO9BGNfxO_pytkSxpANEg==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0t8c9cj1bFYTmlwmCAGGgjyoXQ7F5wpI3ZW5GMpWWXIXZQ2MNKaLlrl42UI9oKn4V20piahbjAeNVgQ5ulaFOKgHZS6xZtiUY96bkbgbjkGoLYByfDqDgrgFtCPMCbg7O_EySL8pGRaTGfFsbpLFpTplLZvJLUcE6cyasSWqxBvyvftd0JzRf0cYHCbA=)\n[7] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHFVBxwEPMKqhN3KP958BsCSe54hUHGICH7tarpBOmIhFnC_guUvnVQAyC1-nnU4PTOb-rjFvlg-ekbHmxzqfsGRp7fPb4i3ce_9didBNSmzG52Dlh9UFjv3py8DvuzrlwYNsLmhfjEZ_-uWzE9K2t9QH7o9QiMWR4Ao8t4H8I97jVfIvnoqbF5DAufsWyoG0B61dwxrl-qMAAbmX2b0CPyLa2chV6PGPc=)\n[8] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFmwbzbdI22woCQdlhR-I08iLCCiSK888neXoqhQPowysETTSLTem9XER1kiQDQaRvkBHopXaLAHqbddd1Thoq-DJWI0jIdnY_Gz-57YjfmnWSc9yG_rJNUygNv-0U_ZrD9driAtgLqSTyBvV4wm6np9byzqQqm8PItRJO__VIRt6ygRFo_43uL6J4V48pvUpvf99fQ9n7Sbg==)\n[9] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQELnfAL-Wb924umRHItvNkc1KgIeoLF1cME2RLQ5BX1T4EbNUUw5WG2Zjs1guU2FfOWhVtEhfSBuN6KoW