          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "[react-ghost](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/react-ghost) [Apr 21, 2022](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYVcQSgEaf4C-faMzfIoCjznqndJN1B7OneECzhvqA-bNBf3ZN6q145gz0JmWTCwKEpgRM58wLWYXdMKj42nEst_BofzMEeEiKUJCl2mQECEozd1JHir-sYA4yL_kc1sM8lFqPkp2bdXAzsd8=#discussion-4025884)"
          }
          text: "[react-ghost](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/react-ghost)\n[Apr 21, 2022](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYVcQSgEaf4C-faMzfIoCjznqndJN1B7OneECzhvqA-bNBf3ZN6q145gz0JmWTCwKEpgRM58wLWYXdMKj42nEst_BofzMEeEiKUJCl2mQECEozd1JHir-sYA4yL_kc1sM8lFqPkp2bdXAzsd8=#discussion-4025884)\n-\nWhen attempting to establish a realtime subscription via a useEffect hook in react-native, I am hit with this message\nTypeError: Invalid URL: undefined\n\n```\nTypeError: Invalid URL: undefined\n```\n\nI don\'t understand why this would happen here as I am successful in making calls to my database in every form, insert, create, update, delete etc.\nI am ONLY hit with this message right now when calling on the realtime database.\nI have no useful error message to diagnose the problem, other than the slight amount of traceability offered by the screenshot that is posted below. I can see from this screenshot that the issue is coming from:\n\\node_modules\\whatwg-url-without-unicode\\lib\\URL-impl.js (21:13)\n\n```\n\\node_modules\\whatwg-url-without-unicode\\lib\\URL-impl.js (21:13)\n```\n\nThe lines of code in this file are:\n\n```\nconst parsedURL = usm.basicURLParse(url, { baseURL: parsedBase }); if (parsedURL === null) { throw new TypeError(`Invalid URL: ${url}`); }\n```\n\n\n```\nconst parsedURL = usm.basicURLParse(url, { baseURL: parsedBase }); if (parsedURL === null) { throw new TypeError(`Invalid URL: ${url}`); }\n```\n\nTo Reproduce Here is what my client setup looks like:\n\n```\nimport { SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_API } from \"@env\"; import { createClient } from \"@supabase/supabase-js\"; import AsyncStorage from \"@react-native-async-storage/async-storage\"; const supabase = createClient(SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_API, { localStorage: AsyncStorage, detectSessionInUrl: false, }); export { supabase };\n```\n\n\n```\nimport { SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_API } from \"@env\"; import { createClient } from \"@supabase/supabase-js\"; import AsyncStorage from \"@react-native-async-storage/async-storage\"; const supabase = createClient(SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_API, { localStorage: AsyncStorage, detectSessionInUrl: false, }); export { supabase };\n```\n\nIn a react context, I am utilizing a useEffect hook to call this line:\n\n```\nuseEffect(() => { const sub = supabase.from(\'favorites\').on(\'*\', (payload) => console.log(payload)).subscribe(); return () => supabase.removeSubscription(sub); }, [])\n```\n\n\n```\nuseEffect(() => { const sub = supabase.from(\'favorites\').on(\'*\', (payload) => console.log(payload)).subscribe(); return () => supabase.removeSubscription(sub); }, [])\n```\n\nThis context provider wraps the root of my app, which is a method I\'ve used before. I have tried moving around the provider to different parts of the app. At first, I maybe thought this was being called before supabase was initialized but it appears to make no difference where the provider is. I have ensured that replication is on.\nWhat\'s more weird is that the Supabase web UI is showing me that Realtime connection requests are being made - I can see this in my dashboard that has stats pertaining to API calls, auth request etc. etc.\nBeta Was this translation helpful? [Give feedback.](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYVcQSgEaf4C-faMzfIoCjznqndJN1B7OneECzhvqA-bNBf3ZN6q145gz0JmWTCwKEpgRM58wLWYXdMKj42nEst_BofzMEeEiKUJCl2mQECEozd1JHir-sYA4yL_kc1sM8lFqPkp2bdXAzsd8=)\n[GaryAustin1](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/GaryAustin1)\n[Apr 21, 2022](https://github.com/orgs/supabase/discussions/6522#discussioncomment-2611288)\nCan you look in your supabase object returned from the client init and see what the base url is? If there is an extra character like /n I believe Supabase.js still works, but I know storage.js does not. Realtime.js also may not handle it. [#5819](https://github.com/supabase/supabase/issues/5819)\n[View full answer](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYVcQSgEaf4C-faMzfIoCjznqndJN1B7OneECzhvqA-bNBf3ZN6q145gz0JmWTCwKEpgRM58wLWYXdMKj42nEst_BofzMEeEiKUJCl2mQECEozd1JHir-sYA4yL_kc1sM8lFqPkp2bdXAzsd8=#discussioncomment-2611288)"
        }
      }
