      chunks {
        position: 20
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          text: "[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)\nAll views and tables in the exposed schema and accessible by the active database role for a request are available for querying. They are exposed in one-level deep routes. For instance the full contents of a table people is returned at\n\n```\nGET /people HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people\"\n```\n\nThere are no deeply/nested/routes. Each route provides OPTIONS, GET, HEAD, POST, PATCH, and DELETE verbs depending entirely on database permissions.\nNote\nWhy not provide nested routes? Many APIs allow nesting to retrieve related information, such as /films/1/director. We offer a more flexible mechanism (inspired by GraphQL) to embed related information. It can handle one-to-many and many-to-many relationships. This is covered in the section about [Resource Embedding](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#resource-embedding).\n\n```\n/films/1/director\n```"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 21
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Horizontal Filtering (Rows)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#horizontal-filtering-rows)"
          }
          text: "[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#horizontal-filtering-rows)\nYou can filter result rows by adding conditions on columns. For instance, to return people aged under 13 years old:\n\n```\nGET /people?age=lt.13 HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people?age=lt.13\"\n```\n\nYou can evaluate multiple conditions on columns by adding more query string parameters. For instance, to return people who are 18 or older and are students:\n\n```\nGET /people?age=gte.18&student=is.true HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people?age=gte.18&student=is.true\"\n```"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 22
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Horizontal Filtering (Rows)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#horizontal-filtering-rows)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_3
            text: "Operators[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#operators)"
          }
          text: "[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#operators)\nThese operators are available:\nAbbreviation\nIn PostgreSQL\nMeaning\neq\n=\n\n```\n=\n```\n\nequals\ngt\n>\n\n```\n>\n```\n\ngreater than\ngte\n>=\n\n```\n>=\n```\n\ngreater than or equal\nlt\n<\n\n```\n<\n```\n\nless than\nlte\n<=\n\n```\n<=\n```\n\nless than or equal\nneq\n<> or !=\n\n```\n<>\n```\n\n\n```\n!=\n```\n\nnot equal\nlike\nLIKE\n\n```\nLIKE\n```\n\nLIKE operator (to avoid [URL encoding](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) you can use * as an alias of the percent sign % for the pattern)\n\n```\n*\n```\n\n\n```\n%\n```\n\nilike\nILIKE\n\n```\nILIKE\n```\n\nILIKE operator (to avoid [URL encoding](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) you can use * as an alias of the percent sign % for the pattern)\n\n```\n*\n```\n\n\n```\n%\n```\n\nmatch\n~\n\n```\n~\n```\n\n~ operator, see [Pattern Matching](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#pattern-matching)\nimatch\n~*\n\n```\n~*\n```\n\n~* operator, see [Pattern Matching](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#pattern-matching)\nin\nIN\n\n```\nIN\n```\n\none of a list of values, e.g. ?a=in.(1,2,3) \342\200\223 also supports commas in quoted strings like ?a=in.(\"hi,there\",\"yes,you\")\n\n```\n?a=in.(1,2,3)\n```\n\n\n```\n?a=in.(\"hi,there\",\"yes,you\")\n```\n\nis\nIS\n\n```\nIS\n```\n\nchecking for exact equality (null,true,false,unknown)\nfts\n@@\n\n```\n@@\n```\n\n[Full-Text Search](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#fts) using to_tsquery\nplfts\n@@\n\n```\n@@\n```\n\n[Full-Text Search](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#fts) using plainto_tsquery\nphfts\n@@\n\n```\n@@\n```\n\n[Full-Text Search](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#fts) using phraseto_tsquery\nwfts\n@@\n\n```\n@@\n```\n\n[Full-Text Search](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#fts) using websearch_to_tsquery\ncs\n@>\n\n```\n@>\n```\n\ncontains e.g. ?tags=cs.{example, new}\n\n```\n?tags=cs.{example, new}\n```\n\ncd\n<@\n\n```\n<@\n```\n\ncontained in e.g. ?values=cd.{1,2,3}\n\n```\n?values=cd.{1,2,3}\n```\n\nov\n&&\n\n```\n&&\n```\n\noverlap (have points in common), e.g. ?period=ov.[2017-01-01,2017-06-30] \342\200\223 also supports array types, use curly braces instead of square brackets e.g. :code: ?arr=ov.{1,3}\n\n```\n?period=ov.[2017-01-01,2017-06-30]\n```\n\nsl\n<<\n\n```\n<<\n```\n\nstrictly left of, e.g. ?range=sl.(1,10)\n\n```\n?range=sl.(1,10)\n```\n\nsr\n>>\n\n```\n>>\n```\n\nstrictly right of\nnxr\n&<\n\n```\n&<\n```\n\ndoes not extend to the right of, e.g. ?range=nxr.(1,10)\n\n```\n?range=nxr.(1,10)\n```\n\nnxl\n&>\n\n```\n&>\n```\n\ndoes not extend to the left of\nadj\n-|-\n\n```\n-|-\n```\n\nis adjacent to, e.g. ?range=adj.(1,10)\n\n```\n?range=adj.(1,10)\n```\n\nnot\nNOT\n\n```\nNOT\n```\n\nnegates another operator, see [Logical operators](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)\nor\nOR\n\n```\nOR\n```\n\nlogical OR, see [Logical operators](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)\n\n```\nOR\n```\n\nand\nAND\n\n```\nAND\n```"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 23
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Horizontal Filtering (Rows)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#horizontal-filtering-rows)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_3
            text: "Operators[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#operators)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_3
            text: "Logical operators[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_3
            text: "Pattern Matching[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#pattern-matching)"
          }
          text: "### Operators[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#operators)\nlogical AND, see [Logical operators](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)\n\n```\nAND\n```\n\nFor more complicated filters you will have to create a new view in the database, or use a stored procedure. For instance, here\342\200\231s a view to show \342\200\234today\342\200\231s stories\342\200\235 including possibly older pinned stories:\n\n```\nCREATE VIEW fresh_stories AS SELECT * FROM stories WHERE pinned = true OR published > now() - interval \'1 day\' ORDER BY pinned DESC, published DESC;\n```\n\nThe view will provide a new endpoint:\n\n```\nGET /fresh_stories HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/fresh_stories\"\n```\n\n### Logical operators[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)\n[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#logical-operators)\nMultiple conditions on columns are evaluated using AND by default, but you can combine them using OR with the or operator. For example, to return people under 18 or over 21:\n\n```\nAND\n```\n\n\n```\nOR\n```\n\n\n```\nor\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /people?or=(age.lt.18,age.gt.21) HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people?or=(age.lt.18,age.gt.21)\"\n```\n\nTo negate any operator, you can prefix it with not like ?a=not.eq.2 or ?not.and=(a.gte.0,a.lte.100) .\n\n```\nnot\n```\n\n\n```\n?a=not.eq.2\n```\n\n\n```\n?not.and=(a.gte.0,a.lte.100)\n```\n\nYou can also apply complex logic to the conditions:\n\n```\nGET /people?grade=gte.90&student=is.true&or=(age.eq.14,not.and(age.gte.11,age.lte.17)) HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people?grade=gte.90&student=is.true&or=(age.eq.14,not.and(age.gte.11,age.lte.17))\"\n```\n\n### Pattern Matching[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#pattern-matching)\n[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#pattern-matching)\nThe pattern-matching operators (like, ilike, match, imatch) exist to support filtering data using patterns instead of concrete strings, as described in the [PostgreSQL docs](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-matching.html).\n\n```\nlike\n```\n\n\n```\nilike\n```\n\n\n```\nmatch\n```\n\n\n```\nimatch\n```\n\nTo ensure best performance on larger data sets, an [appropriate index](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/pgtrgm.html#id-1.11.7.44.8) should be used and even then, it depends on the pattern value and actual data statistics whether an existing index will be used by the query planner or not."
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 24
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Horizontal Filtering (Rows)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#horizontal-filtering-rows)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_3
            text: "Full-Text Search[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#full-text-search)"
          }
          text: "[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#full-text-search)\nThe fts filter mentioned above has a number of options to support flexible textual queries, namely the choice of plain vs phrase search and the language used for stemming. Suppose that tsearch is a table with column my_tsv, of type [tsvector](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/datatype-textsearch.html). The following examples illustrate the possibilities.\n\n```\nfts\n```\n\n\n```\ntsearch\n```\n\n\n```\nmy_tsv\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /tsearch?my_tsv=fts(french).amusant HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/tsearch?my_tsv=fts(french).amusant\"\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /tsearch?my_tsv=plfts.The%20Fat%20Cats HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/tsearch?my_tsv=plfts.The%20Fat%20Cats\"\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /tsearch?my_tsv=not.phfts(english).The%20Fat%20Cats HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/tsearch?my_tsv=not.phfts(english).The%20Fat%20Cats\"\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /tsearch?my_tsv=not.wfts(french).amusant HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/tsearch?my_tsv=not.wfts(french).amusant\"\n```\n\nUsing websearch_to_tsquery requires PostgreSQL of version at least 11.0 and will raise an error in earlier versions of the database."
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 25
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Vertical Filtering (Columns)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#vertical-filtering-columns)"
          }
          text: "[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#vertical-filtering-columns)\nWhen certain columns are wide (such as those holding binary data), it is more efficient for the server to withhold them in a response. The client can specify which columns are required using the select parameter.\n\n```\nselect\n```\n\n\n```\nGET /people?select=first_name,age HTTP/1.1\n```\n\n\n```\ncurl \"http://localhost:3000/people?select=first_name,age\"\n```\n\n\n```\n[ {\"first_name\": \"John\", \"age\": 30}, {\"first_name\": \"Jane\", \"age\": 20} ]\n```\n\nThe default is *, meaning all columns. This value will become more important below in [Resource Embedding](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#resource-embedding).\n\n```\n*\n```"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 26
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Tables and Views[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#tables-and-views)"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Vertical Filtering (Columns)[\357\203\201](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlp7pqcMaiVILujkl5VjZZXzDXPQHRahDDEWD0fuM1aFbUwGyJLYF3Wlzv59CldJtbiIO-x-wIv-foLdzuRi8uni_stdKGVWt1f25m5kVyoVlGIZUIs_h3-pAeLmNCbQFPykiYLQ==#vertical-filtering-columns)"
          }
          headers {
