    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGqm6CvKmRgj8cDJc1_eSO79zV18sRj267t4-N2VMdP-0Nzqj7f2wUfXXLYhbW2nZdan6NnkJ1bhxY1lHL-praeBij3WlqNgSLs9MQCcpOioCkL1sMa17P_UEx6ybsQYwTaQiDlNSuD4JABnVoVRB0Um17twKxPI_u2Z5nm8Yg="
      title: "supabase.com"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFqzPAiqN0apY0UvpgTNK0Vpts9RO5VdnbULJfv61UK0Kq-obtiM6jWFgt66u2c3aG-af1ksLraAeocA4UEy4FHXdtoSsqMlkCXGQaFwEXe_1ykAqtojptUeFuEZ7nyqQNT03rEgaybUEUdRSs="
      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "When encountering an \"Invalid path specified in request URL\" error with Supabase, particularly when interacting with tables, it typically indicates an issue with how the API endpoint for your table is being accessed. This error often corresponds to the PostgREST error code `PGRST126`[1].\n\nHere are the most common causes and resolutions for this error:\n\n### Common Causes\n\n1.  **Incorrect Table or Schema Name in URL**\n    *   Supabase automatically generates a RESTful API from your PostgreSQL database schema. The path in your API request URL must precisely match the name of your table in the database, including case sensitivity[2][3][4].\n    *   If your table is not in the default `public` schema, you must include the schema name in the URL (e.g., `https://<project_ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/your_schema/your_table_name`)[4].\n\n2.  **Missing or Incorrect API URL Base**\n    *   The base URL for your Supabase Data REST API is in the format `https://<project_ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/`[2][5]. An incorrect base URL or missing the `/rest/v1/` segment will result in an invalid path[2][5].\n\n3.  **Insufficient Table Privileges**\n    *   For a table to be accessible via the Data API, the roles making the request (e.g., `anon` or `authenticated`) must have the necessary `SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, or `DELETE` privileges granted[3][6]. If these privileges are revoked or not explicitly granted, Supabase may return a `42501 permission denied` error, which can sometimes manifest as an invalid path if access is denied early in the request pipeline[7][6].\n\n4.  **Stale Schema Cache**\n    *   Supabase uses PostgREST, which maintains a schema cache. If you\'ve recently created a new table or modified an existing one, the cache might not have updated yet, leading to the API not recognizing the path[1][8]. While usually automatic, in rare cases, a cache refresh might be needed[8].\n\n5.  **OpenAPI Configuration Disabled**\n    *   If the OpenAPI configuration is disabled for your project but you are attempting to access the API root path, it can also lead to this error[1].\n\n### Troubleshooting Steps\n\n1.  **Verify Table Name and Schema:**\n    *   In your Supabase Dashboard, navigate to the \"Table editor\" to confirm the exact name and schema of your table. Ensure that the table name in your API request URL matches this exactly, paying close attention to case[4].\n\n2.  **Check Your Supabase API URL:**\n    *   Go to \"Settings > API Keys\" in your Supabase Dashboard to find your unique Project URL. Confirm that your API requests are using the correct base URL, which should look like `https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/` followed by your table name[2][5].\n\n3.  **Review Table Permissions:**\n    *   In the Supabase Dashboard, go to \"Integrations > Data API\". Ensure that the `anon` and/or `authenticated` roles have the necessary privileges (e.g., `SELECT`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`) for the table you are trying to access. You can also inspect and grant privileges using SQL queries directly in the SQL Editor[3][6]:\n        \n\nSources:\n[1] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHwuI9EriDO3WKjufczjpcp8Q08FUt93hXfcoo-GOQNvh8UaWi408IO9DGa7HeIt5e95Axa-Iv3M82zjWDIsPfw2GP77jDVatPA0S76tipLplKPcKsherqZCuBhGILhlb6BIzFmw0JXspQkoTeHQavnkZS6VR4vhPT8wg==)\n[2] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFcDDEDkX_CVUe3LEzcmPwVA73R5d9DxpM08Z3bO1oiKkJTkx-rzYqT5-T4XcATjZ_CZRnDWen7qIXUYUXYWyDHuEMgdXZDIT68sg_1O8roQtgCwZdFGtUOvQ4r67DQaw==)\n[3] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGsdr-gzG86mwtt1o3oQOxNETBNn8NPvh1h5Smn55IBcpK5YXDqwKSxg53LPlcJXjxSkuH4MYyfdkhnXz-AsC0KDg793wqZ87rfeZ5GFThBPJ0G1370w4faLKYCSUAihnS7v1x0fcujoyzGUxjp0bk=)\n[4] [drdroid.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEkgAV-4BK6R0cDOlsGkUDfvmat6tERiGaNY2BcePdwskG388Xh-qwk1ypGp6Y12mI3-4a1SIPR9quQh8UN0qOZscCX4LE9fz8fqqfEFusL3cOOk_p9w6ac84RGVCOScBecnRK3SeszTnp0MqxYVCtAlq_r_ch3labboNgeXH2GWt8Jvt9ZiE0Xww==)\n[5] [draftbit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFd9EFw0gqCjpg46c0_PJ072WPIQZmIAbQeTNq4BxL6Tg27gPwO2anM64XtiJMAbD6ERstlB0Ltq_sUzBzKEB9rLdjQcogWbTofd6CaIvE2bZtB-ywYY0hPBl-K_XsGACkzeAc=)\n[6] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE-QRvXYFoP2zN7VnRac_Mbhr4rUqzV5H5atI9MJF3al0Vf83vxz7idjDGA-BTMeq_PTSFOnMAKI_fg1foMfowmnIMJiGPf5ioUgToKlDumhtB6MqRbMKJeOa4iXfTwaLWsEXse_WT8yIBaRNCYrVlcjVArkRm_uoPdUj6RNExMUDxuye0D)\n[7] [supabase.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGqm6CvKmRgj8cDJc1_eSO79zV18sRj267t4-N2VMdP-0Nzqj7f2wUfXXLYhbW2nZdan6NnkJ1bhxY1lHL-praeBij3WlqNgSLs9MQCcpOioCkL1sMa17P_UEx6ybsQYwTaQiDlNSuD4JABnVoVRB0Um17twKxPI_u2Z5nm8Yg=)\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFqzPAiqN0apY0UvpgTNK0Vpts9RO5VdnbULJfv61UK0Kq-obtiM6jWFgt66u2c3aG-af1ksLraAeocA4UEy4FHXdtoSsqMlkCXGQaFwEXe_1ykAqtojptUeFuEZ7nyqQNT03rEgaybUEUdRSs=)"
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
