      }
      chunks {
        position: 12
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Bug report"
          }
          text: "-  I confirm this is a bug with Supabase, not with my own application.\n-  I confirm I have searched the [Docs](https://docs.supabase.com), GitHub [Discussions](https://github.com/supabase/supabase/discussions), and [Discord](https://discord.supabase.com).\n[Docs](https://docs.supabase.com)\n[Discussions](https://github.com/supabase/supabase/discussions)\n[Discord](https://discord.supabase.com)"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 13
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Bug report"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Describe the bug"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "To Reproduce"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Expected behavior"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Screenshots"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "System information"
          }
          text: "## Describe the bug\nPostgREST schema cache does not update when new columns are added to existing tables or when new tables are created. The cache persists stale information despite all documented refresh methods. This makes it impossible to extend the database schema in production.\nError Code: PGRST204 Error Message: \"Could not find the \'column_name\' column of \'table_name\' in the schema cache\"\n\n```\nPGRST204\n```\n\n\n```\n\"Could not find the \'column_name\' column of \'table_name\' in the schema cache\"\n```\n\n## To Reproduce\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\n1. Add a new column to existing table:\n\n```\nALTER TABLE planting_plans ADD COLUMN batch_number TEXT;\n```\n\n1. Verify column exists in database:\n\n```\nSELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name=\'planting_plans\' AND column_name=\'batch_number\'; -- Returns: batch_number \342\234\223\n```\n\n1. Attempt to use new column via PostgREST API:\n\n```\nconst { data, error } = await supabase .from(\'planting_plans\') .insert({ batch_number: \'TEST-123\', /* other fields */ });\n```\n\n1. See error:\n\n```\n{ \"code\": \"PGRST204\", \"message\": \"Could not find the \'batch_number\' column of \'planting_plans\' in the schema cache\" }\n```\n\nAttempted cache refresh methods (NONE worked):\n\n```\n-- Method 1 NOTIFY pgrst, \'reload schema\'; -- Method 2 NOTIFY pgrst, \'reload config\'; SELECT pg_reload_conf(); -- Method 3 GRANT ALL ON TABLE planting_plans TO anon, authenticated, service_role; NOTIFY pgrst, \'reload schema\'; -- Method 4: DROP and recreate ALTER TABLE planting_plans DROP COLUMN batch_number; ALTER TABLE planting_plans ADD COLUMN batch_number TEXT; GRANT ALL ON TABLE planting_plans TO anon, authenticated, service_role; NOTIFY pgrst, \'reload schema\'; -- Method 5: Project restart via Dashboard -- Paused project \342\206\222 Resumed \342\206\222 Still broken\n```\n\nAlso tested: Creating columns via Supabase Dashboard GUI (Table Editor) - same result.\nAlso tested: Creating entirely new table - table not visible to PostgREST at all (404).\n\n## Expected behavior\nWhen a column is added via ALTER TABLE or Supabase GUI:\n\n```\nALTER TABLE\n```\n\n- PostgREST cache should automatically update within seconds\n- NOTIFY pgrst, \'reload schema\' should force immediate cache refresh\n- New columns should be immediately usable via API\n\n```\nNOTIFY pgrst, \'reload schema\'\n```\n\nWhen project is paused/resumed:\n- PostgREST cache should be completely cleared and rebuilt\n\n## Screenshots\n(Attach screenshots showing PGRST204 errors from browser console)\nError from browser DevTools Console:\n\n```\nPOST https://yyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co/rest/v1/planting_plans Status: 400 (Bad Request) { \"code\": \"PGRST204\", \"details\": null, \"hint\": null, \"message\": \"Could not find the \'batch_number\' column of \'planting_plans\' in the schema cache\" }\n```\n\n\n```\nPOST https://yyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co/rest/v1/planting_plans Status: 400 (Bad Request) { \"code\": \"PGRST204\", \"details\": null, \"hint\": null, \"message\": \"Could not find the \'batch_number\' column of \'planting_plans\' in the schema cache\" }\n```\n\n## System information\n- OS: Windows 11\n- Browser: Chrome 120+\n- Version of supabase-js: Latest (@supabase/supabase-js)\n- Version of Node.js: N/A (using Supabase client in browser)\n- Supabase Project:\n\nPlan: Free\nProject ID: pdteqherbfpndfjpghvh\nURL: yyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co\n\n\n- Plan: Free\n- Project ID: pdteqherbfpndfjpghvh\n- URL: yyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co\n- PostgREST Version: (Unknown - using Supabase hosted)\n- Plan: Free\n- Project ID: pdteqherbfpndfjpghvh\n- URL: yyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co\n\n```\npdteqherbfpndfjpghvh\n```\n\n\n```\nyyigfdevvikroeenqott.supabase.co\n```"
        }
      }
      chunks {
        position: 14
        markdown_chunk {
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_1
            text: "Bug report"
          }
          headers {
            type: MARKDOWN_NODE_TYPE_HEADER_2
            text: "Additional context"
          }
          text: "Timeline:\n- Jan 25, 2026: First attempted to add columns via SQL - cache error appeared\n- Jan 25-26: Spent 3+ hours trying every documented solution\n- Jan 26: Tried GUI column creation - still fails with PGRST204\nImpact:\n- Blocks all database schema changes\n- Cannot add new features requiring new columns\n- Development completely halted\n- Workarounds exhausted\nWhat works:\n- Existing columns and tables work perfectly\n- Direct PostgreSQL queries work\n- Only PostgREST API layer affected\nColumns that won\'t appear in cache:\n- batch_number (text)\n- test_notes (text)\n- test_type (text)\n- Previously: include_in_stats (boolean) - also failed\n\n```\nbatch_number\n```\n\n\n```\ntest_notes\n```\n\n\n```\ntest_type\n```\n\n\n```\ninclude_in_stats\n```\n\nOther observations:\n- RLS is properly configured\n- Permissions are granted to all roles\n- Schema is public\n- No special characters in column names\n- Column types are standard (text, boolean)\n\n```\npublic\n```\n\nThis appears to be a persistent bug in PostgREST cache invalidation mechanism for our specific project. Manual cache flush or investigation needed."
        }
      }
