k to local storage upon Cloudinary failure within the `/server.ts` file, where the Cloudinary upload logic is. If the Cloudinary upload fails, I catch the error, log a warning, and then use the local file upload, which will create the file in /public/uploads! This provides a robust, seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Confirming Upload Strategy**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the upload strategy! If Cloudinary is down, the system smoothly falls back to local storage, which is perfectly secure. It will return the local image URL in the response. This guarantees a seamless user experience!\n\n\n"
