    thinking: "**Analyzing Configuration Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'m now digging into `server.ts` to understand how the `isSupabaseConfigured` variable gets its value. I\'ve located the definition within the file and am examining the conditional logic. The goal is to fully understand when and how Supabase is considered configured within the application.\n\n\n**Evaluating Configuration Details**\n\nNow I\'m breaking down the specific conditions determining Supabase configuration. It appears an empty URL or key immediately results in a \'false\' state. I\'ve pinpointed specific placeholder values and formats that trigger a \'false\' return. Additionally, invalid URL protocols or hostnames also negate the configuration. I\'m checking for trailing spaces now.\n\n\n**Investigating Potential Environment Issues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how environment variables influence the configuration. I\'ve realized that the `trim()` operation alone might be insufficient. If quotes or other special characters are present in `SUPABASE_URL` or `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, the application might misinterpret them. I\'m considering scenarios where a user\'s `.env` includes quoted values, which would then be passed to the code, leading to URL parsing errors, or requests to Supabase that fail due to malformed URLs, so let\'s write a function to strip!\n\n\n**Refining Environment Handling**\n\nI\'ve crafted a `cleanEnvValue` function to safely strip quotes from environment variables, preventing URL parsing errors. Now, the error message \"Invalid path specified in request URL\" has triggered a deeper look at the URL format. I\'m exploring if the Supabase SDK expects a base project URL (e.g., `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co`), rather than one with the `/rest/v1` path, in the event that the environment configuration is incorrect.\n\n\n**Isolating Core URL Behavior**\n\nI\'ve hit on a great idea regarding the Supabase URL. If the user provides `/rest/v1` in the URL, the SDK will re-append it, which causes a \"invalid path\" error. I\'m now exploring how to automatically extract just the base URL by only keeping the protocol and hostname, e.g. `https://${hostname}`. This will make the application much more robust.\n\n\n**Clarifying URL Construction**\n\nI\'m now writing the logic to handle the Supabase URL and am excited about the progress! I\'ve confirmed the \"Invalid path specified in request URL\" error is directly caused by including a path like `/rest/v1` in the `SUPABASE_URL`. The SDK internally adds this path, resulting in a double path and a failing request. Therefore, I\'m building a robust parser that only keeps the base URL, ensuring the application works correctly even with user errors.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 504574965
    }
