      title: "medium.com"
    }
    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, customizing the dark mode selector, especially for a class-based approach, is achieved using the new CSS-first configuration and the `@custom-variant` directive. This marks a shift from the `tailwind.config.js` file used in previous versions.[1][2][3][4][5][6]\n\nBy default, Tailwind CSS v4\'s dark mode relies on the user\'s operating system preference via `prefers-color-scheme`[1][6]. However, to implement a manual dark mode toggle using a class (e.g., by adding or removing a `.dark` class on the `<html>` element), you need to explicitly define this behavior.\n\nTo set up a custom dark mode selector based on a class, you\'ll add the `@custom-variant` directive to your main CSS file (e.g., `input.css` or `globals.css`):\n\n\n\nSources:\n[1] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHlfUuNbE9EuiyQvfiRtK-165Hl7RGqtOu87jsVmXWoaD4nMNk0ZhiRpPJ5ee7rxXFKvSaiGhB5HOozWlhIyqBh8qYw63-kMjud3c6GcnXOoDtEmi1Jy_eLCs9nI00NHMO__lBoPMERVPWqXhlrABfLSc0=)\n[2] [kitemetric.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG8wqoKCZ7SER5eBygwn2xKhPaMh3RfcmMRhReAWhgaGEva3xdevjoTRNcb3_hh7rSe5VtzPi8zr9U456kosh5KCUMX-Px9-zTSnXMshrBaFqQp_00l3HPPUhYRWU5fU6oKFEdOM_wEpWeuajgtInzNAoFwyvDRRSugRiOfmiY7RJcG-b03RCITjHK1xlnwJA_pkU_c9yA=)\n[3] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHlK7ZLcDER5HoxQhedzeM2a5atz7LbEc3-8r4NXYY3ghfvfx5frpY3ovCXqAlwLutRpk8k7JDUMKMrstB9Zwz09B6sU_NazVuOrmxh7EPkOhnGzKmVWPrUiS4MCYSRSKG1DsL1XnqnINenk_3vlhJnqTPp7kqPB5aabNDtPPL3kytZ8d6iTzUtMG61Ai--02LJqmtF-AXjpMD_ANqSVSIumok-)\n[4] [tailwindcss.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEN169cVHFfiwNi4jPm23k8f9G-eUukYLXpxWP2h3LVwAGdtGBEOYGMe8M9EoAJkDC4koKZ9w3dgI87q83sTsybguLru8oXlcg8YWEMvRhOCua3aTd0na2EoKUiNYCSzJ--uL5baA==)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGvNhJoALbibj52H4NhpypxF-S1W7gOw3siIy34YvvIs00hD