    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF6rDFIJQplu7N6j7erj0RQvE6u3h_KTVYk0ArPsGwPzQ4VpRWz9ZaZR97vjGe1Br6xv7JHVYSi0U7MQ1M8pCBjo7HUoEOeGAhYoevt36XSiiYkAZPzUPKYGWwMKmrbHMb6XOnNoCUXQxioBWr08OequBFJD8Qwfj_1adLLE1FGUgUly83tNKVaqgXdt1kl02aLeS0beBGrtfb2T1OrEpUgHv-d7CJzwRCLqwfk2NCEnQ=="
      title: "medium.com"
    }
    summary: "In Tailwind CSS v4, the implementation of dark mode has shifted to a \"CSS-first\" approach, moving away from JavaScript-based configuration in `tailwind.config.js`. The core mechanism still relies on the `dark` variant, but its activation is now primarily managed through CSS.[1]\n\nKey aspects of dark mode in Tailwind CSS v4 include:\n\n*   **Dark Variant** By default, Tailwind v4 utilizes the `dark:` variant to apply styles when the user\'s system preference is set to dark mode, leveraging the `prefers-color-scheme` CSS media feature.[2][1][3]\n*   **\"dark\" Class for Manual Toggling** To enable manual toggling of dark mode (e.g., via a switch), you define a custom variant in your CSS. This custom variant targets a specific class, most commonly `.dark`, on a parent HTML element such as the `<html>` or `<body>` tag.[2][4][5] This is achieved by adding a rule like `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` to your CSS.[2][6][7] When this `.dark` class is present on the `<html>` or `<body>` element, the `dark:` modifiers within your HTML will become active, applying the dark mode styles.[2][5] JavaScript can then be used to add or remove this `.dark` class to toggle between modes.[4][5]\n*   **Selector Strategy** Tailwind v4 allows you to override the default `dark` variant to use a custom CSS selector instead of the `prefers-color-scheme` media query. This enables flexible control over when dark mode styles are applied, such as when a specific data attribute (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) is present on an ancestor element.[1][3][8] For example, you can use `@custom-variant dark (&:where([data-theme=dark], [data-theme=dark] *));` to activate dark mode based on a `data-theme` attribute.[3]\n*   **Configuration Changes** The `darkMode: \'class\'` or `darkMode: \'media\'` configuration keys found in previous versions of `tailwind.config.js` are no longer used in v4. All dark mode configuration is now handled directly within your CSS file using the `@custom-variant` directive.[1]\n*   **CSS Variables** Tailwind CSS v4 also supports using CSS variables for theme tokens. You can define these tokens using `@theme` and then override their values for dark mode within `@layer base` in your CSS.[1]\n\nSources:\n[1] [tailkits.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEac5ny-J28sHi61qP5hczFp47aJvHxfHnFKcihRE05-9N-qHq-nKJKfUC8XX__jubBE0X-7EKkV115wh9ani41ypQVKoJty83CliJsKNMaJmJRGO1evm_48IAqYsoPB-vQ5JCuM54iNLKVTj-uRKT5YP0=)\n[2] [tailadmin.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHKI8-_8oQF8UMdI1VkvFSt8pEzWaIPbzvCw-AMWguOyAeUZtXD99q09eOZB4niOJJzhmd9uQJa0ahyYWkxXygF3UM3YwZODgBdCIUikbueOJBPrrM_6_aG9huNolciRFAiRYi_p2f8F4N4nCqw)\n[3] [tailwindcss.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHFaJyFC9VbsBTYUXT9u4yuulE4D8mEmkZFJsr3dfITePoRlli2kP2IBuz_MgWsosTIJqERK4ECDEUJtSZBGQR8LAcwMo1yqrqhaIckdltJwHWLZKw2yghAGNBIdNrj-xE=)\n[4] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEOb97jmn3X2ojoYxZNCMXBtExegf3ZiOaK4ZpktiGtkfmkYuvemQ4HvK2o3LaTIUD6Q_Yt770eMvw1sevOyG1i6QfJ_adnfzxagbhbemHMOqzixzgN0uWuxcXnmbCEFkhO1sNus9c66nHHjxNR6MNJj2Y=)\n[5] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGHZStOHzEdDXIqM9PCh5VLk3cFi7FoWglbG-hQnjhRCIZ9JGbz2es4zXdwOkw9Bj_tOp2Uag0JhU3PGcIQGUZLyXKHDL8W4UilaSmJytN9EWBVDLpTzTw0U6eiM2bWN1B5Kt0Mmg==)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHNy8TcbKxCJMH4XXlpEq0BF14QqmFJjIfN2-Djohx05r4bhT50PyLZ3P8Xpdra56_PSm1ZK7sHhdXak7eGONNuq03P_TnScjs0c_Z7VHDVFCWCXhRibET2PCUQ946Qv8XqZ0mIHWFqzbGRzo-6rtNNaG61KoVfQD6YAVv0nloK6FnSixGURyo_e7JVFwSGrHMJWFgoS4npC19m-BQ=)\n[7] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGcP3r2PW1hAfP7uefUrKTNLh2lWVgmu2xgf41fiAjw9udZnMdvCafhfFAxJwb51Dm5JFqdrAU58Q5rueqLW5JnDdHAqnftwpG014VhD_pk0GCAhxq6Ux8eLIgaDUYXrDrq3SD5OFObnIjQn4hlG6WgVTkUiORDPdSqO8spSzZweiEpxHTwAKMRV0juA9BqgHeMhmuFfVFtFOnrd5xq24LCsci5LyG_)\n[8] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF6rDFIJQplu7N6j7erj0RQvE6u3h_KTVYk0ArPsGwPzQ4VpRWz9ZaZR97vjGe1Br6xv7JHVYSi0U7MQ1M8pCBjo7HUoEOeGAhYoevt36XSiiYkAZPzUPKYGWwMKmrbHMb6XOnNoCUXQxioBWr08OequBFJD8Qwfj_1adLLE1FGUgUly83tNKVaqgXdt1kl02aLeS0beBGrtfb2T1OrEpUgHv-d7CJzwRCLqwfk2NCEnQ==)"
