  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Confirmation Logic**\n\nI\'ve introduced state variables, specifically `deleteConfirmId` and `deleteConfirmName`, to handle a custom confirmation modal. Replacing the clunky `window.confirm` with this approach will give us more flexibility. The plan is to set these state variables to trigger the modal.\n\n\n**Designing the Modal**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing a beautiful and accessible modal dialogue, positioned elegantly in the screen\'s center. It will render conditionally based on `deleteConfirmId` and `deleteConfirmName` state. When confirmed, it triggers the delete logic; cancellation resets states. I\'m looking at how `handleDeleteClick` is implemented, to integrate the new design.\n\n\n**Refining State Management**\n\nI\'ve added a `deletingGame` state variable to manage the deletion process\'s ongoing state. Now, `handleDeleteClick` sets `deleteConfirmId` and `deleteConfirmName`, triggering the modal. The `executeDeleteGame` function performs the actual deletion, manages success/error messages, updates the game list, and resets the state.\n\n\n"
